# Consumer receipt export: independent scope guidance

Reviewed base `c761a49c55d125bca48ff38d81b0a9ff6fd5adcf` read only. `base-identity.json` hashes the exact 14 inspected sources. No product, root, saved-account or Astrofolio files edited.

1. **One captured result.** In `ChartCalculator.runChart`, after the existing engine load and local resolution, replace the one full-mode natal `computeChart` call with the delivered `computePortableChart` boundary. Publish its detached chart and immutable serialized envelope together only for the same admitted run. Never rebuild a receipt from the compact presentation chart, legacy summary, displayed text or mutable form. Existing unknown-time endpoint `computeBodies` work remains required for Moon/Sun uncertainty; it is not a second natal calculation. Moon/rising modes may keep their existing path for this bounded slice.

2. **Truthful civil context.** The form explicitly resolves unknown time as **local 12:00**, so use reference `local-noon`; known time uses `supplied-instant`. Leave `sourceInstant` null because the form supplied civil fields, not an original ISO instant spelling. Retain the actual local date/effective time/zone, resolved offset (including seconds expressed as fractional minutes), fold earlier/gap shift-forward policy and flags. Compute gapShiftMinutes from resolved UTC plus the actual resolved offset minus the requested proleptic-Gregorian wall instant, constructed with `setUTCFullYear` to avoid year 0–99 remapping. Do not assume every gap is 60 minutes, infer UTC noon, round LMT, or invent browser ICU/tzdb/provenance versions. SDK context validation is arithmetic consistency, not independent authentication of the host's historical zone data.

3. **Generation fence.** Current `runIsCurrent` checks run ID and profile authority but does not check inputRevision on fresh manual runs. Every field/house edit already advances inputRevision. New receipt data needs a synchronous ref invalidation at that boundary, plus new run, failed run, positions-only load and profile scrub. The click handler must check the captured chart/run/revision and any required profile-origin access generation immediately before the side effect; checking rendered state alone admits stale DOM events. Edits made while a lazy module waits must not publish a newly enabled receipt for obsolete input. Existing textual receipt coordinates and LMT zone use live `city`; this is a concrete reason to avoid reading UI labels for export. Download the prepared bytes without recalculation or reading the current form.

4. **Keep source distinctions.** Full birth-detail share links and admitted opaque saved-chart IDs are recomputed through runChart and may receive a new calculation receipt. Positions-only `#p` imports set chart/computedInput/shareInput null and possess no reconstructible natal input; never enable receipt export or invent birth provenance there. Mixed c+p input is rejected. Current profile-derived origin remains private even after manual edits; its access revocation must synchronously clear the new receipt. Fresh manually typed input has no authenticated-account claim. Do not attach a profile ID, label/name, owner or address to the envelope or download filename.

5. **Optional module graph.** Type-only receipt imports in the island are safe. Keep the public engine/receipt codec behind the new full-mode calculation helper's dynamic import; preserve current engine focus warm-up and keep receipt code out of idle/form-focus, lite and moon/rising paths. Explicitly decide module-download failure behavior with root: a fallback may preserve the normal chart if the helper failed to load before any calculation; do not run a second calculation after portable execution fails and do not retry computation from the export action. Existing ModuleLoadError/reload behavior should remain recognizable. No saved-record-store import or new global authority/storage layer.

6. **Existing save/share semantics.** Keep commitSave and its profile generation fence, aggregate v1 wire shape, matching by actual house system, chart count, naming prompt, sync and post-chart events intact. Richer saves remain inactive. The new file download does not alter image sharing, positions/details links, hide-birth-details checkbox or current share dialog. Place it in the existing full-mode More actions disclosure, not a new primary CTA. Export explicitly contains private birth details and a draft calculation record; disclose that next to the action. Do not claim verified birth time, broad numerical certification, a redacted diagnostic or an industry standard.

7. **Copy and access.** Add the required per-page catalog keys consistently for en/es/pt/fr/it/ru. Use an explicit localized text button with type=button, disabled state while unavailable/busy, an associated privacy note, polite status for initiation, and a fixed localized error with no raw cause. Keep native keyboard disclosure behavior and visible focus. Do not announce that the file was saved to disk merely because an anchor click was initiated. Check 320/390 widths, 400% native zoom, reduced motion, and return focus; avoid design or baseline changes.

## Executed baseline context controls

`time-context-probe.mjs` bundles the actual frozen base resolver and delivered portable calculation codec. Seven controls pass on Node22.23.2 (runtime ICU/tzdb recorded), preserving null sourceInstant. These are reference controls, not acceptance of the author's future patch and not broad astronomical/date-range certification. The probe uses synthetic coordinates consistently; it tests time-context consistency, not city matching.

- New York ordinary, one-hour spring gap, and earlier fall fold.
- Lord Howe `2024-10-06 02:15`: resolved `2024-10-05T15:45:00.000Z`, offset +660, gap **30** minutes.
- Apia unknown-time local noon on skipped `2011-12-30`: resolved `2011-12-30T22:00:00.000Z`, offset +840, gap **1440** minutes, local-noon reference and absent houses.
- Mexico City `1907-07-06 08:30`: resolved `1907-07-06T15:06:36.000Z`, offset **−396.6** minutes, no gap.
- Year0099 UTC preserves its century in the library contract; this does not expand the UI's separate date range.

## Frozen browser acceptance plan

Use an exact frozen source/build identity in disposable Chrome, no production/user data. Observe an actual JSON download and parse it with the pinned SDK. Compare the file to the displayed result's UTC, requested/actual houses, uncertainty and flags; assert no form input or network side effects. Cover known ordinary, unknown local noon, DST gap/fold, LMT, polar fallback; required requested placidus/actual whole must survive. Assert no export on positions-only, invalid input, stale form edits or delayed completion. Hold the helper request, edit or revoke profile access before release, then ensure no stale receipt/download. Capture a stale button reference and dispatch after edit to prove the synchronous guard. Exercise a replacement valid run after failure and ensure the newly downloaded file contains only that run. Verify initial/focus/module graph and helper-load failure behavior, all six localized actions/privacy notes, keyboard/zoom layout, Blob URL cleanup and unchanged v1 save behavior using synthetic storage only. Do not duplicate the author's complete suite or reserved Astrofolio work.
